STUDIO HELPER
=============

What this is
-------------
A tool that sets up your print and digital files correctly, names
and organizes everything, and checks your exports before they go to
print or online. It never touches your actual design - only Illustrator,
Photoshop, and Figma do that.


BEFORE YOU EXTRACT THE ZIP
---------------------------
Windows blocks files downloaded from the internet until you tell it
they're OK. Do this once, before you extract:

  1. Right-click the zip file.
  2. Choose Properties.
  3. At the bottom, tick "Unblock", then click OK.
  4. Now extract the zip (right-click -> Extract All...).

If you forget this step, Studio Helper's own Setup check page will
remind you.


STARTING STUDIO HELPER
------------------------
Double-click "Start Studio Helper" inside the extracted folder. Your
browser will open a page - that page IS Studio Helper. You can leave
it open while you work.

The first time you start it, it will show a "Setup check" page that
tells you if Illustrator, Photoshop, and your jobs folder are ready.
Follow any "fix" hints it shows.


ONE-TIME FIGMA SETUP
----------------------
If you use Figma for digital work:

  1. Open Figma desktop.
  2. Go to Plugins -> Development -> Import plugin from manifest...
  3. Pick the file: figma-plugin\manifest.json (inside this folder).

You only need to do this once.


IF ILLUSTRATOR AUTOMATION FAILS
----------------------------------
Sometimes Illustrator won't let Studio Helper control it directly
(a permissions issue, or it's busy). When that happens, use the
manual path instead - Studio Helper will show you these same steps
on screen:

  1. In Studio Helper, click "Open scripts folder".
  2. In Illustrator: File -> Scripts -> Other Script...
  3. Pick the .jsx file Studio Helper told you to run.
  4. When it asks, select the job.json file for your job.

Everything still gets checked and named correctly - only the "click
one button in the browser" part is skipped.


UPDATING
---------
Easiest: on the Home page, click "Check for updates", then "Download
& install" if one is available. Studio Helper downloads the new
version from GitHub, verifies it, and restarts itself into it - no
browser, no manual zip/unzip. This is the only thing in Studio Helper
that ever goes out to the internet, and only when you click it.

Manual alternative: extract the new zip (anywhere) and start it from
there. Your jobs, settings and job history are kept safely in your
Windows user profile and are not affected by updating either way.


QUESTIONS OR SOMETHING LOOKS WRONG
-------------------------------------
Use the "Copy diagnostics" button inside Studio Helper (on the Job
page) and send the file it creates. It contains no client artwork -
just logs and the job's own settings.
